+# dsh-side patches
+
+Patches here are applied to the **host** (the dsh checkout / install tree), not
+to this plugin. They exist because a documented plugin capability still needs a
+general-purpose harness change that official extension points do not provide.
+Keep a patch until the harness ships the seam; a plugin-side fallback does not
+retire it.
+
+## 0001-ui-layout-runtime-product-title.patch
+
+- **Target**: `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` (`0a53fb55be`), package
+  `packages/client/ui-layout`.
+- **Why**: alpha.2 makes `ui-layout` own `document.title` (`DocumentTitle`
+  writes `<session title> — <productTitle>`), but the product title is only the
+  build-time `process.env.DSH_CLIENT_TITLE` or the localized local-build label.
+  There is no runtime extension point, so a plugin whose brand comes from a
+  live settings card can only race the shell by writing `document.title`
+  directly; whenever the shell re-renders a session title it overwrites the
+  configured brand. This patch adds the missing general-purpose seam:
+  `ctx.documentTitle.contribute(owner, title)`.
+- **What it changes**:
+  - adds `ui-layout/src/client/document-title.ts` —
+    `DocumentTitleController` / `IDocumentTitle`, a stacked, owner-scoped
+    contribution source (`getSnapshot`/`subscribe` + `contribute`), last live
+    contribution renders, an empty title contributes nothing, disposal restores
+    the previous contribution;
+  - provides it as `ctx.documentTitle` from `ui-layout`'s `apply`;
+  - binds it into AppFrame's inject face (`hooks: { productTitle }`) so the
+    frame re-renders on contribution changes;
+  - resolves the product title as
+    `contribution ?? DSH_CLIENT_TITLE ?? t('brand.localBuild')`;
+  - updates the `ui-layout` and `ui-brand-official` READMEs (EN + zh) and
+    re-records both `README.i18n.yaml` pairs with the new blob hashes
+    (`pnpm run verify-translation-pairing --write`), so the bilingual-pair gate
+    stays green;
+  - updates the `ui-layout` tests.
+- **Apply** (from the dsh checkout root):
+
+  ```sh
+  git apply /path/to/plugins/patches/0001-ui-layout-runtime-product-title.patch
+  pnpm --filter @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-layout bundle   # rebuild the client row
+  ```
+
+  A source checkout picks the change up with its normal build; an installed
+  tree needs the rebuilt `lib/client.js` (the browser half is served from the
+  install tree, not from `src`).
+- **Rollback**: `git apply -R <patch>`, then rebuild the package. The patch
+  only touches `ui-layout` (plus its two READMEs and the
+  `ui-brand-official` cross-reference).
+- **Upstream adoption**: the harness requires an Agent Note and `doc-sync` for
+  a change of this shape; the patch here is the minimal seam, not the full PR.
+- **Report**: `.dsh-migrate/patch-reports/runtime-product-title/report.md`.
+
+## Verification record
+
+- `git apply --cached --check` against the pristine `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2` index:
+  applies clean; `git apply -R --check` against the patched tree: exact match
+  (re-run after the `README.i18n.yaml` hunks were added).
+- `DocumentTitleController` executed directly from the patched source with
+  Node 24's TypeScript type stripping (the only import is type-only and
+  erased); behavior checks (stable snapshot identity, last-wins, dispose
+  restores, repeated disposer, empty title, throwing-subscriber isolation)
+  pass.
+- Not run: the repository gates (`pnpm run test:gui`, `pnpm run typecheck`,
+  `pnpm run doc-sync`, `pnpm run build`) — this checkout has no dependencies
+  installed and this task did not install them. Run them before sending the
+  patch upstream.
